WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.783
Seventy-six per cent.

2
00:00:01.783 --> 00:00:03.837
That is how much of INS Vikrant,

3
00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.707
the largest warship ever built in India,

4
00:00:05.707 --> 00:00:07.609
comes from Indian sources.

5
00:00:08.009 --> 00:00:09.913
It is about two hundred and sixty-two

6
00:00:09.913 --> 00:00:12.595
metres long, sixty-one metres wide,

7
00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:15.590
and weighs about forty-five thousand tonnes.

8
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.483
The Navy's own bureau designed it;

9
00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.640
Cochin Shipyard built it.

10
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.944
Planes take off up a curved ski-jump

11
00:00:21.944 --> 00:00:24.939
ramp and land by hooking arrester wires.

12
00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:27.027
The Navy calls this STOBAR.

13
00:00:27.428 --> 00:00:29.123
It can carry up to thirty aircraft,

14
00:00:29.123 --> 00:00:31.991
including MiG-29K fighters like this one,

15
00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:34.090
and several kinds of helicopter.

16
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.419
Its special steel,

17
00:00:35.419 --> 00:00:36.708
about thirty thousand tonnes,

18
00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:38.356
came from SAIL.

19
00:00:38.356 --> 00:00:40.132
More than five hundred and fifty Indian

20
00:00:40.132 --> 00:00:43.488
firms, including about a hundred small businesses,

21
00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:44.914
supplied parts.

22
00:00:45.314 --> 00:00:47.137
The name is old.

23
00:00:47.137 --> 00:00:50.318
The first Vikrant retired in nineteen ninety-seven;

24
00:00:50.318 --> 00:00:52.802
the new one was commissioned at Kochi

25
00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:54.856
in September twenty twenty-two.

26
00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.288
For GS Three,

27
00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:58.645
Vikrant is the case study for defence

28
00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:01.815
indigenisation: design, steel and shipbuilding,

29
00:01:01.815 --> 00:01:03.171
all done at home.

